{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2218","id":5277054166,"node_id":"PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABOol01g","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2218","diff_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2218.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/2218.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2218","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2218/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/2218/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/2218/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/210e396d7cb88525c21e91438ecdaa569536a3a3","number":2218,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Refs KS-2173: the Vote delegated log call logs the delegation id alone, not both wallet addresses","user":{"login":"kksecura","id":258699643,"node_id":"U_kgDOD2txew","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura","html_url":"https://github.com/kksecura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Refs KS-2173: the Vote delegated log call logs the delegation id alone, not both wallet addresses\n\n**TIER 2: one log call's meta object in the governance service, a new red-first test file, and a flow and a cheat fragment. No governance decision, vote power, delegation record, database write or response changes.** Merge to develop only. This is part 1 of the ticket (the `Vote delegated` call); the ticket stays open for its part 2, so this PR says `Refs`.\n\nLinear: https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-2173\n\n## Summary\n\n- **What changes.** In `Blockchain/Dev/services/governance/src/services/governanceService.ts`, `delegateVote` logged `Vote delegated` with `{ delegationId, delegatorAddress, delegateAddress }` (lines 1234 to 1238 at develop `bba80c3c8e24`), so every delegation wrote both wallet addresses into the service log. A wallet address is the data subject's own data (`KS-1955`). The call now logs `{ delegationId: delegation.id }` alone (lines 1235 to 1237 after this change), with one why-and-ticket comment line above it. Wednesday's ruling on the shape: the two addresses go, and no other id is added, because whether a participant id is personal data is not measured. So `delegatorId` and `delegateId` are NOT in the meta.\n- **The new test file** `services/governance/src/__tests__/ks2173-vote-delegated-log-holds-no-wallet-address.test.ts` runs the real `delegateVote` over a small `../db` dispatcher (two participant reads by id, one active-delegations read that returns no rows, one delegation save; any other statement is refused) and a `../utils/logger` that records every call at every level. Two controls pass before and after: the call is reached exactly once and saves once (so the other cells cannot pass vacuously), and the delegation record still keeps both addresses. Two test cells fail against the unchanged code: the meta holds neither wallet string, and the meta is the delegation id alone with no wallet string in any logged call.\n- **Not claimed.** The other two layers the ticket names (the request log `Request received` in the governance `index.ts`, and the shared `errorHandler` in `packages/shared`) are part 2 and are not in this PR. The delegation RECORD keeps both addresses (lines 1223 and 1225 at develop); that is stored state, unchanged, and a control cell pins it. No live log was read: production's log level and log store are unmeasured.\n- **Overlap with `PR 2099`.** That open PR edits `governanceService.ts` in two other places (hunks at old lines 603 to 613 and 1206 to 1211; this change starts 23 lines after the second). It was gated, in a scratch object store and never in a working tree, against `PR 2099`'s head `8967de8b1755` before the push: `git merge-tree --write-tree` read rc 0 in both orders with the same merged tree; every changed line of both sides survives (26 distinct changed line values checked, 0 off) and the `KS-2060 round 2` guard appears once; a planted edit inside each of its two hunks (develop lines 607 and 1209) conflicts, rc 1, in both orders; twin edits at lines 900, 1100 and on the call's first line merge, rc 0, in both orders. The push ran under Wednesday's one-push grant for this row, conditional on that gate; `merge-file` was not used.\n\n## Test plan / Test Evidence\n\n**Host and runtime (stated per the repo's test-discipline skill).** Every run below was made on one Apple Silicon Mac (arm64, Darwin 27.2.0), with no Docker stack started (the change is one log call; nothing here reaches a real database or log store). Node is v26.8.1, the only Node on this machine; it is NOT the long-term-support line the repo's `CLAUDE.md` names (Node 24 today), nothing was run on Node 24, and the long-term-support status of Node 26 was not checked. Load1 at the starts was 2 to 3.\n\n**Touched:** four files, base develop `bba80c3c8e24` (the squash of `PR 2212`): `governanceService.ts` (+2 -3), the new test file (+116), and the new flow and cheat fragments `KS-2173-the-vote-delegated-log-call-holds-no-wallet-address.html` (+18 and +4). The census at the cut (GraphQL, 102 open pull requests, 456 file rows, positive and negative controls pass) finds one open PR on the product file (`PR 2099`, above) and none on the other three paths.\n\n**Ran** (by Seat R 114th, 2026-11-12, in tree `s-r114-ks2173`; evidence `evidence/row49/`):\n- **The governance runner, first on an existing cell:** the `KS-1940` file, 24 tests passing, before any number below was relied on.\n- **The new test file against the UNCHANGED product file:** 4 tests, 2 failed (the two test cells), 2 passed (the two controls). **With the change:** 4 passed. **The call planted back** with `delegatorAddress: delegator.walletAddress`: the same 2 cells fail again, and the file was restored byte for byte afterwards.\n- **The whole `services/governance` suite:** 20 suites and 367 tests before, 21 suites and 371 tests after, all passing.\n- **docs-fragments check:** OK without the pair and OK with it (flow 117 legacy + 237 new, cheat 112 legacy + 237 new); I added the pair because the skill's section 4 owes it for a test change. **`npm run audit:gate`:** OK (5 distinct advisories reported, 5 baselined). **`npm run check:test-types`:** exit 0 (five services, not governance). **`eslint`** on the product file and the new test file (absolute paths): exit 0, no output.\n\n**NOT run:** the other services' suites; the four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, k6); any run against the live demo or the local Docker stack; Node 24; any CI run (retired for this repo). The pre-push hook's legs (below) run the repo's checks on the pushed head.\n\n**Migrations + config:** none.\n\n**Pre-push hook:** (quoted from the push of this head)\n```\nPREFLIGHT INCOMPLETE — 13/16 legs ran, 3 SKIPPED. Nothing failed.\n  legs 3 4 8 — local stack not up; you can clear this by starting it.\n  This is NOT a pass. Do not quote it as one — say which legs ran.\n```\n- Leg 14, verbatim: `shell suites: 127 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (of 127)`\n\n## Before this deploys\n\n- Nothing deploys from this PR. The change is in the governance service, so it ships with that service's next image build; it reaches develop only, and \"deployed\" reads as \"on develop\".\n\n## Notes for the gate\n\n- **The behaviour that matters:** what `delegateVote` hands the logger. The response, the saved delegation and every other log call in the function are unchanged.\n- **What the proof does not see.** The cell reads a recording logger, not the real log transport; it does not read the other log calls in the service, the request log or the shared error handler (part 2).\n- Branch name `feature/ks-2173-governance-the-vote-delegated-log-line` is Linear's own suggestion for the ticket.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T12:04:40Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T12:04:46Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"80757e056b51c86726b3fc414b3e563b2441db7b","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Secuura:feature/ks-2173-governance-the-vote-delegated-log-line","ref":"feature/ks-2173-governance-the-vote-delegated-log-line","repo":{"id":1170327089,"node_id":"R_kgDORcHGMQ","name":"Distributed_Secuura","full_name":"Secuura/Distributed_Secuura","owner":{"login":"Secuura","id":257240886,"node_id":"O_kgDOD1UvNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura","html_url":"https://github.com/Secuura","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/